
  CAVEAT ON ARM 3: this is a SCALAR LUT walk, not the AVX2 kernel
  (aegis_core::ops::ternary_matvec_serial). It is therefore a LOWER
  BOUND on the engine's streaming rate, not the engine's rate. Compare
  it to the technical report's 'achieved' bandwidth row, which is itself
  a derivation from a cycle count and an unstated nominal clock.

  The decode roofline must divide by the TERNARY figure, not the peak.
  Quoting a single-thread peak as 'the machine bandwidth ceiling' both
  understates the machine and overstates the kernel's share of it.
  This run is one machine, one buffer size, one pattern. It replaces an
  unsourced number with a measured one; it does not make it a ceiling.
